'''Royal Titans Changes'''

* Players can now exchange Giantsoul Amulets with the Odd Old Man for 30 Big Bones each.
* World 567 is now the suggested Royal Titans world.
* The enrage slam animation is no longer delayed by a tick on certain occasions.
* Fixed a bug where a Titan’s body disappeared upon death, its base persisted after respawning, and ice remained in the arena for the next fight.
* The Prayer filter will no longer show older Prayer icons after they are upgraded.
* Teleporting out of the Royal Titans boss arena will now nullify any incoming damage to prevent death.
* Tagged minion hitboxes have been scaled down and no longer take up so much space.
* On sacrifice, if a player doesn't receive the pet, a message will appear in the chatbox to say: "You don't feel lucky during your sacrifice".

'''Client and Mobile Updates'''

* The HiScores panel now remembers the previously searched data set.
* Failed HiScore searching now displays new UI and text within the search bar.
* Added a new toggle which allows chat filters to always show, even when chat is collapsed.
* The HiScores popout panel will now auto-open when the player uses the in-world lookup feature.
* Mobile users can now hide split private chat when the chatbox is closed.
* The Barrows Interface no longer gets stuck behind the Minimap interface.
* Adjusted the deadzones around the chatbox and the left side on the mobile client.
* Menus now appear in front of Minimap orbs, and important functions like the close button won't be blocked when they overlap.
* Certain hotkeys with a corresponding checkbox or toggle in the Settings menu now correctly sync to the correct state.
* The loot tracker no longer shows incorrect truncated numbers on the enhanced client.
* When using the hotkey side panel, the buff bar now dodges as it would if the player used the right-side stones.

'''Poll 83 Improvements'''

* Players can now "Reset" birdhouses, allowing you to dismantle an existing birdhouse and automatically build and place a new one. The clockwork mechanism from the previous birdhouse is reused.
* Players can now build and place a birdhouse directly on an empty patch with a single click, provided they have all the necessary tools and materials.
* Both of the above changes will use pre-made birdhouses you carry with you before attempting to make one out of bits.
* Net traps used to catch Salamanders can now be reset automatically.
* Players can now trade in duplicate Hunter Guild uniques with Verity in exchange for a reroll on the Master Sack loot table (excluding uniques and the pet).
** Eligible items include: Enhanced Quetzal Whistle Blueprint, Perfected Quetzal Whistle Blueprint, Huntsman's Kit, or any of the four Guild Hunter gear pieces.
* When using the Alchemy spell on the Explorer’s Ring, Runes will now be used from your Inventory before consuming the Ring’s daily charges. If no Runes are available, the Explorer’s Ring will automatically provide the necessary charges to cast the spell.
* Enchant Jewellery will now convert the first jewellery in the Inventory, rather than the specific jewellery it was cast on.

'''Other Changes'''

* The Pendant of the Ates now includes all minimenu teleport sub-options
* Camera shake effects for the following events can now be toggled on or off in the settings: Baba Yaga's house, Fishing Trawler, Looted Barrows chests, Lizardman Shaman jumps, Great Olm's falling crystals, Falling rocks in the Monkey Madness tunnels.
** Note: If you turn the camera shake off in the Monkey Madness tunnels, you will still be warned of impending crushing doom by a shadow briefly appearing under your character before rocks fall, providing a clearer visual cue for incoming damage.
* Reviewed and corrected recolouring inconsistencies across the game. As a result, some NPCs and locations have received slight visual adjustments. Most notably, the Blessed Sickle is brighter than before, making it easier to distinguish from its non-blessed variant.
* Fixed a bug that occurred when switching out a Draynor Manor teleport from a teak portal.
* Fixed a bug where Verac's set effect was ignoring damage immunity checks.
* You can no longer accidentally get repeat Jad or Zuk tasks by cancelling them through teleport.
* Rewrote the text that appears in your Bank's potion storage when it's empty, aiming to make it a bit clearer.
* The Grouping interface now correctly recognizes when a player has joined the Mage Training Arena chat channel.

