==Royal Titans: A Titanic Success!==
Well, well, well… looks like you lot can’t get enough of fighting massive, furious, elemental juggernauts. Who would've thought?

It’s been awesome seeing players gather at the entrance, teaming up, and working out strategies before diving into battle. Newer players are getting the hang of gear switching and mechanics, while the PvM veterans are pushing the fight to its limits with optimizations we didn’t even expect. One of our biggest goals with this boss was to ease players into gear switching by making it a core part of the encounter - dodging fire and ice, handling minions, and keeping up with changing threats. From what we’re seeing, mission accomplished!

[[File:Royal Titans Feedback & 12th Birthday Celebrations (1).png|thumb|600px|center|''If you can’t see the image above, click [https://cdn.runescape.com/assets/img/external/oldschool/2025/newsposts/2025-02-12/Cave.jpg here]!'']]

The Royal Titans fill an important PvM space in the mid-game. Players usually start their PvM journey with Scurrius, Barrows, and Fire Cape attempts before moving into more complex content. The Titans sit comfortably in that progression, helping bridge the gap before stepping into fights like Zulrah. Learning gear-switching and movement mechanics here will set you up nicely for tougher encounters like Raids.

A lot of the mechanics were inspired directly by the community, including the addition of Desiccated Pages, which have been a big hit. You've also enjoyed the new Prayer Scrolls, which are particularly popular among Iron players attempting the Corrupted Gauntlet.

===Bug Fixes and Improvements===
As the dust settles, we’ve taken the time to make some changes based on your feedback:

* Players can now exchange Giantsoul Amulets with the Odd Old Man for 30 Big Bones each.
* World 567 is now the suggested Royal Titans world.
* The enrage slam animation is no longer delayed by a tick on certain occasions.
* Fixed a bug where a Titan’s body disappeared upon death, its base persisted after respawning, and ice remained in the arena for the next fight.
* The Prayer filter will no longer show older Prayer icons after they are upgraded.
* Teleporting out of the Royal Titans boss arena will now nullify any incoming damage to prevent death.
* Tagged minion hitboxes have been scaled down and no longer take up so much space.
* On sacrifice, if a player doesn't receive the pet, a message will appear in the chatbox to say: "You don't feel lucky during your sacrifice".

There are some other points of feedback we’d like to address today.

''Minion Attack Delay Adjustments''

Right now, when minions are killed, the Titans’ attack delay is reduced - one tick per minion. If all three are taken out at once, the next attack happens three ticks sooner. Some players have suggested removing this delay entirely, but we feel that could be a bit too strong. For now, we’re happy, but we’re keeping an eye on it.

''Looting Mechanics''

Soloing the fight? You’ll still only get one set of loot. If you're taking the titans down as a pair, your regular loot and unique chances will scale depending on your damage contribution. This boss was designed with duo play in mind, and we wanted to take a key learning from Scurrius by calculating pet rolls without taking contribution into account. In short, the more Titans you take down, the better your odds of getting the pet!

''Entry Restrictions''

Once the Titans’ HP drops below 85%, no new players can enter the fight. This prevents issues with reward distribution, protects GIM prestige, and ensures future Combat Achievement balance, but it is something we'll continue to think about.

''Grouping System''

No official grouping system is planned, but we’ve allocated four Royal Titans worlds and updated the grouping Clan Chat world to make finding a partner easier. And if all else fails, there’s always the community Discord!

''Future Use for Giantsoul Amulets?''

Many of you have asked if extra Giantsoul Amulets will have another purpose. Well, we know an NPC who knows a thing or two about bones... and the Odd Old Man is always interested in a good trade!

The Royal Titans have brought a fresh and engaging mid-level PvM experience to Old School RuneScape, and we’ve loved seeing players take on the challenge. We’ll continue monitoring feedback and making adjustments where needed, but for now, keep the discussions going, keep refining your strategies, and most importantly - keep taking on the Titans!

==The Big 1-2! A Livestream Birthday Bash to Behold…==
Old School RuneScape is turning 12 this month! While the in-game event arrives next week, we’re kicking off the festivities early with some chaotic, nostalgic, and maybe even cake-fueled activities. Join us on '''February 20th from 16:30 to 18:00 GMT''' over on the [https://www.twitch.tv/oldschoolrs OldSchoolRS Twitch channel] for a celebratory livestream!

===J-Mod Castle Wars: Ultimate Escort Edition===
We’re taking your classic Castle Wars experience and turning it into something truly chaotic. Two J-Mods will battle it out in a special Castle Wars game mode, with Mods Kieren and Rice acting as your team’s not-so-subtle secret weapons. They’re walking, talking, tanky targets!

Here's the breakdown:

* At the start of the game, the enemy J-Mod will yeet themselves (technical term) directly into your base to steal your flag. Rude.
* But these ain't no ordinary J-Mods... Their HP will be buffed to the nines and they'll be tankier than a full Justiciar enjoyer at the Inferno, so don’t expect them to be an easy takedown.
* Your mission? Defend your base by preventing the enemy J-Mod from escaping, or race to the rescue and escort your J-Mod home safely!

J-Mod Rules:

* J-Mods must walk only - no running allowed!
* J-Mods can only start moving at the 18-minute mark, giving you and your team time to build up a strategic defence.
* J-Mods can attack you back, including Chins and Barrage! So watch your back and be ready with those protection Prayers.
* J-Mods will pick their gear before the match starts - so no sneaky swaps mid-game.
* Underground tunnels are off-limits to J-Mods… unless they want to be obliterated by falling rocks.

===Bake Off: Gielinor Edition===
Got a sweet tooth and a love for all things OSRS? Bake an OSRS-Themed Birthday Cake for our competition and be in with a chance to win some amazing prizes! You’ve got until February 17th to put on your Cooking Gauntlets and whip up a cake worthy of the gods (or at least one that won’t get insta-binned by the Lumbridge Cook).

* When? February 10th (09:00 GMT) to February 17th (21:00 GMT)
* Submit your culinary creations to the [https://osrs.game/Discord-Birthday-Cakes #birthday-cakes] channel on Discord or post them on [https://www.reddit.com/r/2007scape/comments/1im25ak/competition_bake_an_osrsthemed_birthday_cake/ Reddit].

The top three cakes will be shown on stream, and Twitch chat will pick the ultimate winner!

A grand prize for the Champion Baker includes:

* A RuneScape Kingdoms: Shadow of Elvarg board game
* A RuneScape Cookbook
* A whole YEAR of membership

